Replaced the linear scan with a binary search over the sorted `mesgs` table, cutting lookup cost from O(MESGS) to O(log MESGS). The lower-bound form still returns the first matching entry, matching the original behavior.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    int lo = 0;
    int hi = MESGS;

    while (lo < hi)
    {
        const int mid = lo + ((hi - lo) >> 1);

        if (mesgs[mid].num < num)
            lo = mid + 1;
        else
            hi = mid;
    }

    if (lo < MESGS && mesgs[lo].num == num)
        return &mesgs[lo];

    return NULL;
}
```